course: dictionary
lesson: 12716
title: The back of the body
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: A dorsum is a noun for the back or upper surface of a part of the body, such as the back of the hand or the top of the foot. Doctors and scientists use it when they need an exact word. «The nurse cleaned the dorsum of my hand before the injection.» The nurse cleaned the top of the hand, the side you see when your palm faces down.
explain: The word can also mean the back of an animal. «The frog had a bumpy dorsum covered in green spots.» Here the dorsum is the whole top side of the frog, from its head to its back legs.
explain: Use context to check. Read the words around dorsum: if the sentence talks about a hand, a foot, a tongue or an animal's back, it probably means the back or top surface. Swap in the word back or top and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Dorsum is a noun. Its plural is dorsa.
fact: «Dorsum» means the back or upper surface of a body part, or the back of an animal.
fact: «The dorsum of the foot» is the top of the foot, the part you see when you point your toes.
fact: «Dorsal» is related to dorsum, as in the dorsal fin of a shark, which sticks up from its back.
fact: Doctors and scientists use dorsum in notes and diagrams, so you will meet it most in science and medicine.
exercise: «The nurse cleaned the dorsum of my hand before the injection.» What does dorsum mean here? | *The back or top surface of the hand | The fingertip | The palm, the side you hold things with | The wrist bone
exercise: Which word is related to dorsum, and is used for the fin on a shark's back? | knuckle | *dorsal | palm | plantar
exercise: «The sun made the dorsum of his foot go red.» Where is the dorsum? | *On the top of the foot | In the heel | Under the sole, where you walk | Between the toes
test: «The frog sat on the log with a spotted dorsum.» What is the dorsum of the frog? | Its tongue | Its back legs only | *The back of the animal | Its belly underneath
test: What is the plural of dorsum? | *dorsa | dorsums | dorsus | dorsi
exam: «The vet pointed to the dorsum of the cat's paw.» Where is the dorsum? | *On the top surface of the paw | Between the claws | In the cat's ear | Under the paw, on the pads
